course: dictionary
lesson: 3305
title: Ethnic: groups and cultures
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ethnic is an adjective. It is about a group of people who share a culture, traditions, a language or family history. The clue is the word group: ethnic tells you something about a whole group, not about one person.
explain: Ethnic can also describe things that come from a culture, such as food, clothes or music, especially from another country. When you see «ethnic food», think: food from a particular culture, probably one that is different from the one around you.
explain: Your sentence uses a very serious term: «"Ethnic cleansing" means driving out or killing a whole ethnic group from an area.» This is a cruel crime, and you will learn about it in history lessons when you are older, with a teacher. For now, keep the core idea: an ethnic group is a group that shares roots, language or customs.
fact: Ethnic means to do with a group that shares culture, traditions, language or family history.
fact: An ethnic group is a group of people who share these things, such as language or customs.
fact: An ethnic minority is a smaller group of people within a country, with its own culture or language.
fact: «Ethnic background» means the family roots and culture a person comes from.
fact: «Ethnic food» means food from a particular culture, often from another country.
exercise: Ethnic means to do with what? | The weather in one town | *A group of people who share a culture, language or family history | A single person's favourite colour | A type of sport
exercise: Ayesha says «ethnic food» means food that is always spicy. What does ethnic tell us here? | Food that is cooked outdoors | Food that is always spicy | *Food from a particular culture, often from another country | Food that nobody is allowed to eat
exercise: «Ethnic minority» is a phrase in social studies. Which best describes an ethnic minority? | The largest group in every country | *A smaller group within a country, with its own culture or language | A group of people who all live in the same house | A team of sports players
test: What does «ethnic background» tell us about someone? | Their favourite lesson at school | Their score in a test | *Their family roots and culture | Their height and weight
test: Which is the best example of ethnic food? | A packet of crisps from the corner shop | A plain bowl of cereal eaten at home in a hurry | Ice cream from a van | *Injera, a flatbread from Ethiopia
exam: Which sentence uses ethnic correctly? | She ran ethnic around the playground | *She cooked an ethnic meal from her grandmother's country | He put the ethnic on his desk | The ethnic rain fell all afternoon
